      "widgets_values": [
        "Premium digital drawing for the SAME illustrated book as image4. Portrait1024x1536. INPUT ROLES: image1 approved shared physical SCALE plate, image2 Shir identity/outfit, image3 Skitters hatchling identity, image4 approved page STYLE and SAFE FRAMING. Keep warm pale cream, moss green, soft hand-drawn contours and luminous ordinary garden. Shir nine, blue eyes, honey dark blonde topknot at scalp apex, normal child head proportions, lilac shirt, dusty rose shorts, pink patterned fabric sport sandals with black soles/connectors. Pink backpack: three HUNTR/X girls print ONLY on rear panel; front torso view shows straps/plain pink side, never rear print. Skitters same small puppy-sized HATCHLING every page: light turquoise, butter yellow belly, apricot wing undersides, amber eyes, ivory horn buds, golden forehead star; four legs TWO wings ONE tail. Scale image1 is authoritative: Shir130cm, dragon shoulder18cm, snout-to-rump30cm excluding20cm tail, headtop approx36cm. Never enlarge dragon for composition or shrink for a sandal. Same ground depth. Full figure composition closely matches approved image4 framing: Shir scalp/bun no higher than40% image height, soles around85%; dragon head about73%, paws85%. Quiet pale almost empty UPPER38% for HTML text. Bottom12% empty path; ALL essential bodies/tails/contact within central60% width. No text, lettering, diagrams, panels, speech bubbles. Ordinary stone garden path and shrubs, subtle warm glow, no fantasy flowers or beings, no door unless requested. One clear story moment. Gentle humor. Shir SITS on garden path left with knees bent naturally, backpack still on her back, suddenly ducks her head and raises one forearm a little defensively. Skitters right sits at SAME actual scale, mouth slightly open in tiny innocent BURP, no flame or smoke or drawn sound marks. His innocent surprised face contrasts her overreaction. Keep Shir seated anatomy and dragon size physically anchored: dragon head below seated Shir shoulder, body puppy sized. More upper quiet space from seated pose; do not enlarge figures to fill.",
